                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Very fun game that has some of the better graphics I have seen in VR.  The art style and sci fi theme are the real strong points here.  The gameplay is that of a wave shooter that mimics an arcade style light gun game but in 360.  There are mini guns and grenade launchers and shotguns available but you have to find them during the level and they run out of ammo quickly so you mostly use dual pistols for the whole game. I had a blast playing it.  There are some unlocks you can get and over thirty achievements, so there is some reason to replay it.  The gun upgrades are pretty much cosmetic from what I can tell.  The game feels very polished for a VR title up until you finish ~stage 6 and the story comes to a hault.  The game states that there are plans to add more content soon.  That being said, you can play the training missions and shoot balls or repeat the story levels on harder difficulty.  I beat it on novice and played 25 levels of training in about an hour and a half.  So that should give you an idea of what you get for your money as of 8/4/17.  I really did enjoy this game and can't wait to see more content for it.  If you could only get one game today and wanted a wave/cover shooter then I would reccomend overkill VR at this time as it is more polished.  If you already own that and want more games like it or want something more like Ghost in the Shell (the anime, not the poorly written movie) then this is a fun game to play through.  It really does feel like being a part of a sci fi universe.  And the voice acting and graphics are pretty good.  I give it 2 thumbs up if they add more levels and content.",
